The first up is DataprocCreateClusterOperator; this operator will create  
a Dataproc cluster. You can specify the cluster configuration using a json string, like this:
CLUSTER_NAME = 'ephemeral-spark-cluster-{{ ds_nodash }}'
cluster_config_json = {
    «worker_config": {
      «num_instances": 2
    }
}

All files with this format will be written as configurations when we run the terraform 
command. 
In the backend.tf file, write the following script in Cloud Editor, and don't forget to 
change the bucket name to your own GCS bucket:
terraform {
  backend «gcs» {
    bucket = «packt-data-eng-on-gcp-data-bucket»
    prefix = «terraform-backend-basic»
  }
}
This script will configure Terraform to use a GCS bucket to store the configuration 
files in the GCS bucket, in a folder that's stated in the prefix, which in this example is 
terraform-backend-basic.

